# Keep `docker/openclaw/` Docker-build uploads small. The Dockerfile's
# build context is the repo root (so it can COPY both `docker/openclaw/`
# and `packages/openclaw-bridge-plugin/`), but most of the repo isn't
# relevant to the image — exclude aggressively.

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
**/bun.lock
**/package-lock.json
**/pnpm-lock.yaml
**/yarn.lock

# SST + Pulumi state
.sst
**/.sst

# Build outputs (we only want packages/openclaw-bridge-plugin/dist/ —
# everything else is irrelevant to the OpenClaw container)
**/.turbo
**/.next
**/.open-next
**/coverage
microservices/**/dist
packages/web/dist
packages/api-utils/dist
packages/db/dist
packages/ui/dist
packages/eslint-config/dist
packages/typescript-config/dist

# Git
.git
.gitignore

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
.cursor
.claude
.zed

# Tests + tooling that doesn't belong in the image
**/__tests__
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/vitest.config.ts
**/eslint.config.js
**/.eslintrc*

# Env files (never bake secrets into the image)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Temporary / scratch
.#*
docs/handoff
.claude/worktrees
